{"packet_id":"D065-01","doc_id":"D065","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"screening_restrictions","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Fair Chance in Housing Act criminal record screening limits","requirement":"A housing provider may not ask about an applicant's criminal record before making a conditional offer, and after an offer may consider only specified convictions within set lookback periods; arrests without conviction, expunged, pardoned, vacated, juvenile and sealed records are excluded.","key_value":"No inquiry before conditional offer; 6-year, 4-year and 1-year lookbacks by offense degree","coverage_conditions":"A dwelling unit offered for rent by a housing provider for residential purposes; excludes a dwelling unit in an owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units.","applicability":{"conditions":[{"type":"owner","role":"exempt","who":"owner-occupied","unit_limit":4}],"per_tenancy":null,"coverage_quotes":["“Rental dwelling unit” means a dwelling unit offered for rent by a housing provider for residential purposes, other than a dwelling unit in an owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units."]},"exemptions":"A dwelling unit in an owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units; a provider may consider a methamphetamine-manufacture conviction in federally assisted housing and a lifetime sex offender registration requirement.","penalty":"Director may impose penalties up to $1,000, $5,000 or $10,000 depending on prior violations, order cease-and-desist, remediation, return of the application fee, and payment to the applicant of up to $1,000.","effective_date":"2022-01-01","valid_through":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 46:8-55","quoted_span":"A housing provider shall not make any oral or written inquiry regarding an applicant’s criminal record prior to making a conditional offer.","interaction":null,"relations":[],"confidence":0.95,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D065-01","doc_id":"D065","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"application_screening_fees","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Fair Chance in Housing Act application fee disclosure and refund","requirement":"Before accepting any application fee, a housing provider must disclose in writing whether its eligibility criteria include criminal history review and that the applicant may submit evidence of inaccuracies, rehabilitation or mitigating factors; the director may order the fee returned.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"A dwelling unit offered for rent by a housing provider for residential purposes; excludes a dwelling unit in an owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units.","applicability":{"conditions":[{"type":"owner","role":"exempt","who":"owner-occupied","unit_limit":4}],"per_tenancy":null,"coverage_quotes":["“Rental dwelling unit” means a dwelling unit offered for rent by a housing provider for residential purposes, other than a dwelling unit in an owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units."]},"exemptions":"A dwelling unit in an owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units.","penalty":"The director may require that the applicant’s rental application fee be returned.","effective_date":"2022-01-01","valid_through":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 46:8-55","quoted_span":"Prior to accepting any application fee, a housing provider shall disclose in writing to the applicant:","interaction":null,"relations":[],"confidence":0.85,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D065-01","doc_id":"D065","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Fair Chance in Housing Act eviction after overturned director order","requirement":"If a housing provider's successful appeal overturns a director's order that placed an applicant in a unit, that determination is grounds to evict the former applicant, so long as the provider gives at least 45 days' notice.","key_value":"45 days' notice","coverage_conditions":"A former applicant residing in a rental dwelling unit owned by the housing provider as the result of the director's order; a dwelling unit in an owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units is excluded.","applicability":{"conditions":[{"type":"owner","role":"exempt","who":"owner-occupied","unit_limit":4}],"per_tenancy":"Eviction of a former applicant housed under a director's order that a court later overturns on the housing provider's successful appeal.","coverage_quotes":["evict the former applicant if that person resides in a rental dwelling unit owned by the housing provider as the result of the director’s order","“Rental dwelling unit” means a dwelling unit offered for rent by a housing provider for residential purposes, other than a dwelling unit in an owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units."]},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":"2022-01-01","valid_through":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 46:8-63","quoted_span":"shall be grounds for the housing provider to evict the former applicant if that person resides in a rental dwelling unit owned by the housing provider as the result of the director’s order, so long as the housing provider provides the applicant with at least 45 days’ notice prior to the eviction","interaction":null,"relations":[],"confidence":0.85,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D065-01","n_rules":3,"note":null}

